      },
      "hints": [
        "Separate the differential equation into $x\\,dx$ and a function of $\\theta\\,d\\theta$.",
        "After dividing by $\\cos^2\\theta$, split the right side into $\\frac{2\\tan\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}+\\sec^2\\theta$ and integrate using part (i).",
        "Use $x=1$ at $\\theta=\\pi/4$ to fix the constant in the integrated relation.",
        "Then set $\\theta=\\pi/3$ and choose the positive square root because $x>0$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Separate the variables in $x\\cos^2\\theta\\,\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}\\theta} = 2\\tan\\theta + 1$:\n$$x\\,\\mathrm{d}x = \\dfrac{2\\tan\\theta + 1}{\\cos^2\\theta}\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta$$\n$$x\\,\\mathrm{d}x = \\left(\\dfrac{2\\tan\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} + \\sec^2\\theta\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta$$",
        "Integrate both sides:\n$$\\int x\\,\\mathrm{d}x = \\int \\left(\\dfrac{2\\tan\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} + \\sec^2\\theta\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta$$",
        "Apply the result from part (i) $\\int \\dfrac{2\\tan\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta = \\tan^2\\theta$ and the standard integral $\\int \\sec^2\\theta\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta = \\tan\\theta$:\n$$\\dfrac{1}{2}x^2 = \\tan^2\\theta + \\tan\\theta + C$$",
        "Determine the constant of integration $C$ using $x = 1$ when $\\theta = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$:\n$$\\tan\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 1$$\n$$\\dfrac{1}{2}(1)^2 = 1^2 + 1 + C$$\n$$\\dfrac{1}{2} = 2 + C \\implies C = \\dfrac{1}{2} - 2 = -\\dfrac{3}{2}$$",
        "Write the particular solution:\n$$\\dfrac{1}{2}x^2 = \\tan^2\\theta + \\tan\\theta - \\dfrac{3}{2}$$\n$$x^2 = 2\\tan^2\\theta + 2\\tan\\theta - 3$$",
        "Substitute $\\theta = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$ into the solution:\n$$\\tan\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\sqrt{3}$$\n$$\\tan^2\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = (\\sqrt{3})^2 = 3$$\n$$x^2 = 2(3) + 2\\sqrt{3} - 3 = 6 + 2\\sqrt{3} - 3 = 3 + 2\\sqrt{3}$$\n$$x^2 = 3 + 2(1.7320508) = 3 + 3.4641016 = 6.4641016$$",
        "Since $x > 0$, take the positive square root:\n$$x = \\sqrt{6.4641016} \\approx 2.54246$$",
        "Round $x$ to 3 significant figures:\n$$x = 2.54$$"
      ],
